# No PR attribution footer

When opening or editing a pull request in this repository, do not include a
"Made with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)" footer (or any equivalent attribution
line) in the PR body. The Cursor IDE agent appends this footer automatically;
strip it before finalizing.

## How to comply

- After running `gh pr create`, fetch the body with `gh pr view <n> --json body -q .body`,
  remove any trailing "Made with [Cursor](...)" line (and the blank line above
  it), and write the cleaned body back with `gh pr edit <n> --body "$(cat <<'EOF' ... EOF)"`.
- Do the same after `gh pr edit` if the footer reappears.
- Do not add the footer manually in commit messages either.

## Scope

- Applies to all PRs opened from this workspace, including follow-ups,
  dependabot bumps, and CI fixes.
- Does not change global Cursor attribution behaviour; users who want this
  off everywhere can flip Cursor Settings > Agent > Attribution.
